<h2 id="fast-dev-workflows-for-agents-too" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter"><span>Fast dev workflows for agents, too</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#fast-dev-workflows-for-agents-too" aria-label="Link to Fast dev workflows for agents, too"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h2>
<p>AI agents do not want long-lived infrastructure - they want databases they can spin up instantly, use while a task is running, and shut down when they are done.</p>
<p>Neon&#x27;s model maps cleanly to that way of working. That is why Neon is the Postgres of choice for <a class="" href="https://neon.com/case-studies#ai">agentic platforms</a> and why we&#x27;re even offering a <a class="" href="https://neon.com/programs/agents#agent-plan-pricing">dedicated Agent Plan</a> designed for these workloads.</p>
<p><span aria-owns="rmiz-modal-" data-rmiz=""><span data-rmiz-content="not-found" style="visibility:visible"><img alt="Agent-friendly database lifecycle with Neon" loading="lazy" width="704" height="447" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="rounded-lg" style="color:transparent;width:100%;height:100%" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fuse-cases%2Ffast-dev-workflows%2Fagent-database-lifecycle-workflow.png&amp;w=750&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 1x, /_next/image?url=%2Fuse-cases%2Ffast-dev-workflows%2Fagent-database-lifecycle-workflow.png&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 2x" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fuse-cases%2Ffast-dev-workflows%2Fagent-database-lifecycle-workflow.png&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7"/><span class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 z-10 border border-black mix-blend-overlay dark:border-white rounded-lg" aria-hidden="true"></span></span></span></p>
<section class="quote my-8 border-l-2 border-green-44 pl-6"><figure class="flex flex-col gap-5"><blockquote class="max-w-[710px] border-none p-0 font-mono text-xl leading-snug font-normal tracking-extra-tight text-black-pure dark:text-white sm:text-lg">&quot;<!-- -->Neon turns a database into something an agent can actually use. Spin it up, load data, reason over it, shut it down when the task is done. That is exactly how agents want to work<!-- -->&quot;</blockquote><figcaption class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2.5"><div class="flex items-center gap-2.5"><div class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-full"><img alt="Rick Blalock" loading="lazy" width="32" height="32" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="pointer-events-none m-0 size-8 rounded-full object-cover sm:size-7" style="color:transparent" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2F_next%2Fstatic%2Fmedia%2Frick-blalock.09rvdvvsqnog3.jpg&amp;w=32&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 1x, /_next/image?url=%2F_next%2Fstatic%2Fmedia%2Frick-blalock.09rvdvvsqnog3.jpg&amp;w=64&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7 2x" src="/_next/image?url=%2F_next%2Fstatic%2Fmedia%2Frick-blalock.09rvdvvsqnog3.jpg&amp;w=64&amp;q=75&amp;dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7"/></div><div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 text-base leading-snug tracking-tight"><span class="font-medium text-black-pure dark:text-white">Rick Blalock</span><span class="font-normal text-gray-new-40 dark:text-gray-new-70">—</span><cite class="font-normal text-gray-new-40 not-italic dark:text-gray-new-70">Co-founder at Agentuity</cite></div></div></figcaption></figure></section>
<p>What makes Neon so fitting for agents:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Postgres that agents can deploy and manage.</strong> With Neon, agents can provision Postgres databases programmatically via API, without manual sizing, capacity planning, or configuration work.</li>
<li><strong>Large fleets != large costs.</strong> Those same databases scale down to zero when inactive, so deploying thousands of rarely used databases does not become a cost concern.</li>
<li><strong>Branches for checkpoints and versions.</strong> Agents can use branches and snapshots to maintain versioned states of an app or workflow, or to offer restore and rollback features directly to end users.</li>
<li><strong>A full backend via SDKs.</strong> For full-stack agents, Neon also provides <a class="" href="https://neon.com/docs/auth/overview">Auth</a> and PostgREST-compatible APIs, packaged together in a single SDK.</li>
</ul>
